  "boundary": "The actual seventh-order Hartree remainder is locally Lipschitz from the mixed first-order X ball to classical Cartesian H1, including the zero increment and the weak derivative identities. All source samples and their bounds are derived from the original fields. The background is real C1, L4 and bounded, with bounded/L2 differential; background L2 is not assumed. The constrained propagator, high Sobolev local flow, physical reconstruction and full main theorem remain unconstructed. This mixed X is not the manuscript homogeneous H1/intersect H25/16 graph space; no embedding of that graph space into X is claimed. Two further actual kernel bounds use density Linfty/intersect L3/2 and differential L1/intersect L25/8; they do not yet identify the non-L1 density derivative or supply the homogeneous Sobolev bridge. The synchronized-slice original environment is revalidated, not added to the historical denominator.",
